Project Idea: Sorting Visualizer (MERN)
Objective

Build an interactive Sorting Algorithm Visualizer using React (frontend) and Node/Express (backend) — where users can:

See how sorting algorithms (like Bubble, Merge, Quick, Insertion, Selection, Heap Sort) work step-by-step.

Adjust speed, array size, and algorithm choice.

See the sorting animation in real-time using colored bars or cards.

Features / User Stories

User can:

See a page header with app title — “Sorting Visualizer”.

See a control panel with options:

Select Sorting Algorithm (dropdown)

Adjust Array Size (slider)

Adjust Speed (slider)

Generate New Array (button)

Start Sorting (button)

View the array represented visually as bars or cards of different heights.

Watch animations showing comparisons and swaps during sorting.

See color cues for:

Comparing elements (e.g., yellow)

Swapping (e.g., red)

Sorted (e.g., green)

Use a clean, modern UI built with TailwindCSS or Material UI.

